  "description": "# Less3 Postman Collection\n\nThis collection is organized into two top-level folders:\n\n- REST: Less3 management, dashboard, administrative, RBAC, reporting, maintenance, and OpenAPI routes.\n- S3: S3-compatible data-plane routes signed with AWS Signature Version 4.\n\nBefore running requests, review the collection variables. For a local Docker/default setup, the defaults are usually enough: baseUrl is http://localhost:8000, adminApiKey is less3admin, tenantId is default, and the S3 access/secret keys are default/default.\n\nREST requests use the x-api-key header by default. To test session-based authorization, run REST > Auth Sessions > Login with User Password or Login with Credential, then replace x-api-key with x-less3-session-token: {{sessionToken}} on the request you want to test.\n\nS3 requests inherit AWS Signature Version 4 auth from the S3 folder. Set s3AccessKey, s3SecretKey, awsRegion, bucketName, and objectKey before running those requests against a non-default server.\n\nCreate/read/update/delete requests use sample IDs in variables such as newBucketId, roleId, permissionId, and requestHistoryId. Update those values if a prior run already created the same record or if you want to target existing resources.\n\nSome requests require IDs that come from list/enumerate responses, such as objectId, authorizationAuditId, uploadId, multipartPartEtag, and versionId. Run the corresponding list/create request first, then copy the returned value into the matching variable."
